        "id": 17096186,
        "title": "Narcan Training at the Library",
        "description": "<p><!-- x-tinymce/html -->Families across the country are dealing with the health, emotional, and economic effects of the opioid epidemic.<strong>&nbsp;The best way to help combat this epidemic is through awareness and education.&nbsp;Together, we can reduce the dangers of opioids and their impact on our communities.</strong>&nbsp;</p>\n\n<p>Stop by the Los Gatos Library to learn how to use Narcan.&nbsp;This training will be a short training on how to recognize the signs of an opioid overdose and administer the opioid overdose reversal drug, naloxone. You will take home a box of Narcan to add to your first-aid kit and new resorces for your community</p>\n\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n\n<p>&nbsp;</p>",
